<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iskandar Thani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1610–1641</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iskandar Thani was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> from 1636 to 1641. A prince of Pahang brought to Aceh after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iskandar-muda">Iskandar Muda</a> conquered his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, he married the sultan's daughter and was chosen as his successor. His short reign was milder than his predecessor's, and he patronised the Gujarati scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuruddin-ar-raniri">Nuruddin ar-Raniri</a>. After his death his widow ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-ul-alam-safiatuddin-syah">Taj ul-Alam Safiatuddin Syah</a>.</p></div>
